WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.291
A site with content in several languages needs a way for visitors to choose one.

00:00:06.291 --> 00:00:10.351
The Content Culture Picker adds a language menu to the site.

00:00:10.351 --> 00:00:14.780
In this video, you will enable it, try it, and set how it behaves.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:22.770
The picker is a menu in the navigation bar of the site.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:27.993
Its button shows the current language, and its menu lists the other supported languages.

00:00:27.993 --> 00:00:30.160
Orchard Core calls them cultures.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:35.250
For the picker to switch pages, the site needs at least two supported

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:41.094
cultures, pages translated with the Localization part, and a path for each page from Autoroute.

00:00:41.094 --> 00:00:45.550
The theme must also show the navigation bar, as The Default Theme does.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.148
When a visitor picks a language, the picker looks for the same page

00:00:50.148 --> 00:00:52.045
in that language and opens it.

00:00:52.045 --> 00:00:55.682
If there is none, it can open the homepage in that language, or

00:00:55.682 --> 00:00:57.580
leave the visitor on the page.

00:01:01.814 --> 00:01:03.681
Let's open Tools, Features.

00:01:03.681 --> 00:01:09.734
The Content Culture Picker is listed under Internationalization, so let's search for content culture.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:16.592
The row describes the picker, and lists its dependencies, Autoroute and Content Localization.

00:01:16.592 --> 00:01:22.920
Autoroute gives each page its path, and Content Localization provides the Localization part.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:24.514
Select Enable.

00:01:24.514 --> 00:01:30.410
A message confirms that the feature Content Culture Picker was enabled, and the row shows Enabled.

00:01:34.618 --> 00:01:36.272
Let's select Visit Site.

00:01:36.272 --> 00:01:40.131
This is the home page in English, and the navigation bar holds a

00:01:40.131 --> 00:01:42.998
menu that shows the current language, English.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:44.917
Let's open the menu.

00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:50.220
It lists the other supported language under its own name, so French appears as français.

00:01:50.702 --> 00:01:51.908
Choose français.

00:01:51.908 --> 00:01:55.856
The picker finds the French version of the home page and opens it.

00:01:55.856 --> 00:02:00.902
The menu shows français as the current language, because the page itself is in French.

00:02:01.377 --> 00:02:04.984
The picker works the same way on every translated page.

00:02:04.984 --> 00:02:08.767
Let's follow the link to the contact page, Nous contacter.

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:10.607
Let's choose English.

00:02:10.607 --> 00:02:14.641
The picker finds the English version of the contact page, and the visitor

00:02:14.641 --> 00:02:15.968
lands on Contact us.

00:02:20.195 --> 00:02:22.778
Some pages exist in one language only.

00:02:22.778 --> 00:02:28.355
On the contact page, let's follow the link to Opening hours, which has no French version.

00:02:28.817 --> 00:02:30.464
Let's choose français.

00:02:30.464 --> 00:02:35.112
The picker finds no French version of Opening hours, so the visitor stays

00:02:35.112 --> 00:02:36.877
on the page, in English.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:47.810
To send the visitor to the homepage instead, open Settings, Localization, Content Culture Picker.

00:02:48.262 --> 00:02:49.973
The page has two options.

00:02:49.973 --> 00:02:54.552
Homepage redirect opens the homepage in the chosen language when the page has

00:02:54.552 --> 00:02:56.428
no version in that language.

00:02:56.428 --> 00:02:57.642
Let's select it.

00:02:58.101 --> 00:02:59.081
Select Save.

00:02:59.081 --> 00:03:02.401
A message confirms that the site settings were updated.

00:03:02.852 --> 00:03:06.481
Let's visit the site again, and follow the link to Opening hours on

00:03:06.481 --> 00:03:07.872
the English home page.

00:03:08.337 --> 00:03:09.924
Let's choose français.

00:03:09.924 --> 00:03:14.401
This time, the picker finds no French version of Opening hours, and opens

00:03:14.401 --> 00:03:16.497
the French homepage, Bienvenue.

00:03:20.695 --> 00:03:23.612
Both settings pages have a Set Cookie option.

00:03:23.612 --> 00:03:27.845
Here, on the Content Culture Picker page, it is selected by default.

00:03:28.296 --> 00:03:32.273
When a visitor picks a language, the picker stores it in a cookie,

00:03:32.273 --> 00:03:35.311
and the site reads that cookie on later requests.

00:03:35.311 --> 00:03:40.006
The cookie lasts 14 days by default, and scripts in the browser cannot read it.

00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:44.080
Let's open Settings, Localization, Content Culture.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.567
Its Set Cookie option is not selected by default.

00:03:48.022 --> 00:03:51.913
When it is selected, the site stores the language of any page with

00:03:51.913 --> 00:03:56.182
a Localization part that a visitor opens, even when they skip the picker.

00:03:56.643 --> 00:04:02.296
Both pages are available only to users who have the Manage ContentCulturePicker settings permission.

00:04:02.296 --> 00:04:04.803
The Administrator role has it by default.

00:04:06.803 --> 00:04:11.058
The Content Culture Picker gives visitors a language menu, and takes them to

00:04:11.058 --> 00:04:13.444
the translation of the page they are on.

00:04:13.444 --> 00:04:14.793
Thanks for watching.

